  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district (FYE Aug 31, 2025); treated as cash. Receipts/disbursements from the governmental funds statement (pp4-6) Total Governmental Funds column. That statement omits the Student transportation row (468,225) although it is in the printed 12,855,255 total; amount taken from General Fund components Total column (p9) and Statement of Activities (p1). Several total-column printed lines are rounded (carline, penalties, homestead, pro-rate) so lines sum to 13,085,453 vs printed 13,085,454. Other local receipts and Other nonrevenue receipts split using the report's own fund schedules. Balance sheet = net position section of the Statement of Activities and Net Position (p3), cash basis. Detail: individual fund budget-and-actual schedules (General p12-14, Depreciation, Employee Benefit, School Nutrition, Special Building, QCPU, Student Fee, Activities); the combining schedules on pp8-11 not recorded to avoid double counting. Bond Fund schedule (p19) has no 2025 activity. Activities fund printed only as a one-line schedule (no per-account detail). General Fund printed Student transportation 648,225 includes a 180,000 transfer to Depreciation Fund (reclass column p10); split into 468,225 expenditure and -180,000 other financing. Printed totals: General Fund expenditure total 10,637,861 includes the 130,000 and 180,000 transfers; Depreciation and Activities revenue totals include transfers in. Blank 2025 actual lines omitted (County fines 2110, IDEA 4512, High ability 3535, EB Benefits paid, Bond principal). Read pages 1-22 of 22."
}